{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms","id":1335043,"title":"A fistful of charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-11T00:58:05-07:00","id":1335043,"title":"A fistful of charms","content":"Something I created, for a modernish story I'm trying to write<br /> <br /> <b>Efficacious Masseuse Technique</b><br /> Medicine: 2<br /> Essence: 1<br /> <br /> The solar knows the acupuncture. He knows the stress points of the body. He knows the places where muscles knot, and cartilage cracks. A solar using this charm carries out a 15 minute dramatic action, where he relieves stress, undos tension, and purifies unclean essence. After this, the target of the charm is relieved of all penalties from fatigue, and regains one temporary willpower. For the rest of the day, the target rolls for fatigue at double the time interval<br /> <br /> <b>Blessed nourishment prana</b><br /> Craft: 2<br /> Essence: 1<br /> <br /> The sun itself is a bringer of light, heat, and life to Creation. And so is the Solar. The charm supplements an action to create food, medicine, or anything which is consumed. The food becomes tasty and nourishing, no matter how poor the starting ingredients were. The food also enhances the one eating it, power coursing through their body as it is digested. For the rest of the day, the eater gains (Solar's essence) of extra dice in any attribute or ability the solar chooses. <br /> <br /> <b>Electronic infiltration methodology</b><br /> Larceny: 3<br /> Essence 1<br /> Some thieves could pick locks. Mortals, in their desire for security, attempt to improve them. There are more things now. Biometric sensors, card readers, and voice detectors. All of which are bypassed the same as any other. One lock is the same as the other, in the eyes of the Solar Exalted. This supplements an attempt to infiltrate a facility, where high tech defenses reside. Here, a Solar can flash a bookshop gift card and have it be accepted, open his eyes to be scanned, press his finger upon the scanner, and still be allowed in regardless of his true credentials. This can be defeated by thaumaturgy. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T01:45:56-07:00","id":1335050,"title":"","content":"All look good in principle. I have a few thoughts?<br /> <br /> What are the costs? Are they committed?<br /> <br /> Any limit to how much Willpower Efficacious Masseuse Technique can restore?<br /> <br /> &quot;Extra dice&quot; means &quot;Charm dice&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> I don't think Solar charms should generally effect all rolls based on a given Attribute.<br /> <br /> Any pre-reqs?<br /> <br /> I'd allow Door-Evading Technique to defeat electronic locks. Granted Electronic infiltration methodology seems to do more than that, but I'd probably pitch it midway between Lock Opening Touch and Door-Evading Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T01:48:51-07:00","id":1335052,"title":"","content":"No comitting, save for the infiltration one. Willpower recovery is only one. Extra dice mean charm dice. <br /> <br /> Pre-reqs? These are low-down. Only an excellency or another charm. <br /> <br /> That's a different thing. Door-evading technique lets you walk through doors and gateways. Electronic infiltration can let you sidle up to the door, tap your bus pass and finger, and you walk in as the VI greets you. Its the difference between being able to infiltrate a palace as a ninja, and walking in as a fake noble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T01:55:45-07:00","id":1335054,"title":"","content":"Only one Willpower... per day? Scene? Ever? Every time the Charm is used?<br /> <br /> Can you chain a two-hour massage session to get 8WP?<br /> <br /> Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise and Door-Evading Technique require Larcency 4. I'm a little wary of pegging Electronic infiltration methodology below this level. Especially as Door-Evading Technique is Essence 3 and Lock-Opening Touch requires a roll to avoid complications. Electronic infiltration methodology seems very powerful.<br /> <br /> It's fine in concept, but as I said, I'd peg it between Lock Opening Touch and Door-Evading Technique. But if you wanted to build it off Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise that'd be appropriate too.<br /> <br /> +5 Dexterity all day is still pretty powerful if the motes aren't committed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-11-2019, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T01:57:14-07:00","id":1335056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335054#post1335054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only one Willpower... per day? Scene? Ever? Every time the Charm is used?<br /> <br /> Can you chain a two-hour massage session to get 8WP?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 willpower a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T05:20:45-07:00","id":1335090,"title":"","content":"I echo many of the above concerns, plus am a tad weirded out by the implications of your Craft one; can you make a literal shit sandwich that boosts the eater\u2019s Socialize? What about stuff that\u2019s generally inedible or even poisonous?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T05:26:50-07:00","id":1335092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335090#post1335090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I echo many of the above concerns, plus am a tad weirded out by the implications of your Craft one; can you make a literal shit sandwich that boosts the eater\u2019s Socialize? What about stuff that\u2019s generally inedible or even poisonous?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an old Werewolf Gift (and possibly a D&amp;D spell) that basically makes inedible crap a nourishing meal. I don't think the premise should be outside the scope of Solar Craft Charms. The exact mechanics are debatable but is a tasty s*** sandwich really a stretch compared to, say Kopi Luwak coffee? Or Ceviche? Or honey? Or chicken periods served sunny side up? Or sausage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-11-2019, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T15:38:29-07:00","id":1335206,"title":"","content":"Isn't Touch of Blissful Relief a pain-relieving Charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T16:53:19-07:00","id":1335215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335090#post1335090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I echo many of the above concerns, plus am a tad weirded out by the implications of your Craft one; can you make a literal shit sandwich that boosts the eater\u2019s Socialize? What about stuff that\u2019s generally inedible or even poisonous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe addendum that the food itself must be normal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T17:13:02-07:00","id":1335219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335092#post1335092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the premise should be outside the scope of Solar Craft Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree to disagree, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335092#post1335092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exact mechanics are debatable but is a tasty s*** sandwich really a stretch compared to, say Kopi Luwak coffee?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Yes.</i> The beans are roasted and ground and held in a filter while boiling water is poured through it; the civet is not directly pooping into your cup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335092#post1335092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Ceviche?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also yes. The lime juice effectively sears the fish, and quick, careful preparation is still key to avoid food poisoning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335092#post1335092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or honey?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still a stretch, yes. Most microorganisms won't grow in honey, even over thousands of years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335092#post1335092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or chicken periods served sunny side up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, still a stretch. We have all kinds of ways of making sure eggs are safe to eat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335092#post1335092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or sausage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, even compared to sausage. We cook sausage, and moreover, make sure the ingredients in it aren't gonna kill the people who eat it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335215#post1335215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe addendum that the food itself must be normal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also not big on being able to stockpile potential five-die buffs with simple mote expenditures, nor that a quick fried egg gives the same dice boost as a difficult meal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-11-2019, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T17:15:07-07:00","id":1335220,"title":"","content":"Where the fuck did the shit sandwich idea come from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T17:16:51-07:00","id":1335221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335215#post1335215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe addendum that the food itself must be normal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe just organic, I\u2019m fine with magic to make poop edible, it\u2019s not the main idea. As you said bonegnawers can make gruel from spit and paper rather easily.<br /> <br /> But I like these, we need chef charms period, and I didn\u2019t know I even wanted a message charm till now. But they don\u2019t cost any essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T18:03:15-07:00","id":1335227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335220#post1335220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where the fuck did the shit sandwich idea come from?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://slate.com/culture/2017/02/the-origins-of-the-phrase-shit-sandwich.html\" target=\"_blank\">According to Slate\u2026</a><br /> <br /> (I suggested it in this thread to be an example of something thoroughly unpalatable and inedible. Feel free to substitute a fine drizzle of Yozi venom and a sprinkle of ground glass on a lump of granite.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-11-2019, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T19:35:03-07:00","id":1335237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335221#post1335221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe just organic, I\u2019m fine with magic to make poop edible, it\u2019s not the main idea. As you said bonegnawers can make gruel from spit and paper rather easily.<br /> <br /> But I like these, we need chef charms period, and I didn\u2019t know I even wanted a message charm till now. But they don\u2019t cost any essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>What message charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T19:41:10-07:00","id":1335238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335227#post1335227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://slate.com/culture/2017/02/the-origins-of-the-phrase-shit-sandwich.html\" target=\"_blank\">According to Slate\u2026</a><br /> <br /> (I suggested it in this thread to be an example of something thoroughly unpalatable and inedible. Feel free to substitute a fine drizzle of Yozi venom and a sprinkle of ground glass on a lump of granite.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh. Just think of it as a charm to enhance simple dishes beyond what they could do. Say, a carrot stew that's surprisingly tasty and delicious, and gives the eater greater strength to go about the day, despite the lack of spices, salt, and vitamins that should have lead to malnutrition.<br /> <br /> Or a sandwich made from cheese and meat that even the butcher didn't want, and you used it as a morning breakfast to get through the entire day while working as a laborer. <br /> <br /> Or tea made from a re-used teabag, that staved off hunger pangs and tastes surprisingly good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T23:49:26-07:00","id":1335263,"title":"","content":"Tireless Solar Work<br /> Integrity: 2<br /> Essence: 1<br /> <br /> The Solar's have much work to do, and yet so little time. The first purchase of this charm, allows the character to go without sleep save for one hour a day. A second purchase at Essence 2 obviates need for sleep at all, save for willpower recovery and doubles the time interval needed for exhaustion. A third purchase at Essence 3 triples the time period, and at Essence 4, the Solar is immune to all possible sources of exhaustion save for magic, whether curse or poison.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 09-12-2019, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T00:19:01-07:00","id":1335269,"title":"","content":"1) Why Athletics? Wouldn\u2019t it fit better in Resistance or Integrity, the abilities for powering through in spite of physical or mental hardship?<br /> <br /> 2) Curses tend to be magical; you shouldn\u2019t have to worry about exhaustion from non-magical curses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T00:23:13-07:00","id":1335270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335269#post1335269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Why Athletics? Wouldn\u2019t it fit better in Resistance or Integrity, the abilities for powering through in spite of physical or mental hardship?<br /> <br /> 2) Curses tend to be magical; you shouldn\u2019t have to worry about exhaustion from non-magical curses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.... true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T05:52:13-07:00","id":1335301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335219#post1335219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree to disagree, I guess.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes.</i> The beans are roasted and ground and held in a filter while boiling water is poured through it; the civet is not directly pooping into your cup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but Craftsman Needs No Tools (which I pressume would be the pre-req) lets you &quot;cook&quot; food with nothing but your bare hands.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's beyond the realm of Solar Charms to sanitize food without tools.<br /> <br /> (Ooo and K\u00e6stur h\u00e1karl. The point is that there are many ways of making food safe to eat.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-12-2019, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T07:16:43-07:00","id":1335306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335237#post1335237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What message charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typo it\u2019s supposed to say massage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T02:27:48-07:00","id":1335433,"title":"","content":"<b><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">Sensitive perception of the healer</span></i></b><br /> Essence: 1<br /> Medicine 2<br /> Prereqs: Flawless diagnosis technique<br /> <br /> The eyes of the sun burn through all lies, filth, and illusions. The Solar can perceive the ailments, maladies, and properties of the body and life before him, rolling Medicine + Perception, with (Essence) auto-successes<br /> <br /> Difficulty 1: Injury, whether from a broken arm, twisted ankle, or such. Sickness, such as the flu<br /> Difficulty 3: The first week of pregnancy. More subtle illnesses such as diabetes or cancer<br /> Difficulty 5: The presence of genes for cystic fibrosis or muscular dystrophy. The propensity for dementia, or the genes for sickle-cell anemia. Generally, diseases with zero outer signs even with modern medicine, such as pancreatic cancer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 10-15-2019, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T07:42:47-07:00","id":1335499,"title":"","content":"Diabetes was actually pretty detectable in the ancient world, provided someone was willing to taste your piss. I definitely wouldn't call it subtle on the same level as the first week of pregnancy.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Indeed, I'd prefer to move the first week of pregnancy down to difficulty 5+, since even modern medicine seldom detects pregnancy until weeks after the fertilized egg takes root.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-13-2019, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T08:11:28-07:00","id":1335508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1335499#post1335499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diabetes was actually pretty detectable in the ancient world, provided someone was willing to taste your piss. I definitely wouldn't call it subtle on the same level as the first week of pregnancy.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Indeed, I'd prefer to move the first week of pregnancy down to difficulty 5+, since even modern medicine seldom detects pregnancy until weeks after the fertilized egg takes root.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn it. My lack of medical knowledge strikes again! <br /> <br /> (seriously though, this is at a glance. You got any good ideas for the difficulty table?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T20:20:52-07:00","id":1336999,"title":"","content":"I've been reading Sandra and Woo. The titular character says &quot;I'll sell my soul for a glass of lemonade!&quot; And it suddenly appears in front of her. She runs away after that. <br /> <br /> Deadly Gift of the Desert<br /> Essence: 3<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp<br /> Prereqs: First Cecelyne Excellency, Transcendent Desert Creature<br /> <br /> Some folks, dig up treasure long buried within the desert sands. Some, find an oasis, deep within the desert, drinking it up and eating the fruits by it. Some, explore long dead catacombs in wastelands, hoping for that one last score. <br /> <br /> Beware of the pile of treasure laid down on the floor before you. For it is a trap. This charm is related to Verdant Emptiness Endowment. Instead of bestowing dots of abilities, it can bestow belongings. As long as the belonging is not greater than anything like a car, and there is sufficient space, the Infernal can conjure any object up to his essence in resources value (No creating jewels at Essence 3). As the Infernal grows in power, the more valuable objects he can conjure. In exchange for this, the Infernal gains a hold over the target. <br /> <br /> At any point in the future, the Infernal may come back to that individual and demand any one task. If the target understands the demand and the task isn\u2019t literally impossible, she intuitively understands that doom will befall her for failing to obey. After one month or as soon as the task becomes impossible (or constitutes an unacceptable order), the duty ends without harm to the beneficiary. However, if the character stops working toward the goal for more than a day while the duty remains, she suffers a number of automatic botches equal to the Infernal\u2019s Essence rating. These botches match the effects of breaking an oath sanctified by an Eclipse Caste Solar and linger until the worst possible time. It is possible to target oneself with the Charm, in which case the Infernal obviously owes himself nothing.<br /> <br /> Mirage of Accursed Kindness<br /> Essence: 5<br /> Cost: N/A<br /> Prereqs: Deadly gift of the desert<br /> <br /> The desert taketh, and the desert giveth. This upgrades its prerequisites. Now, the Infernal can produce far larger things in exchange for wishes. This inclues palaces, houses,cities, libraries, orchards, farms, and forests. A great storm of dust and sand erupts form nowhere, obscuring the location. As it does down and disappears to nothingness, the gift of the Infernal is shown in all its glory. The favour and obligation from the prerequisite still holds true with one alteration. Upon failure to comply, the gift given will be taken back. A fire will erupt and consume the library, turning invaluable scrolls into ash and dust. A rot will consume the orchard, turning once vibrant and delicious fruits into disgusting masses of goo. An earthquake will strike the palace, collapsing it into rubble. Farms will be raided, burned, or the land itself will grow septic and ill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T21:47:19-07:00","id":1337014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026up to his essence in resources value (No creating jewels at Essence 3)\u2026 </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d argue that small gemstones are absolutely acceptable at Resources 3, considering that it\u2019s the baseline stipend for a Realm Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T22:18:24-07:00","id":1337026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1337014#post1337014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d argue that small gemstones are absolutely acceptable at Resources 3, considering that it\u2019s the baseline stipend for a Realm Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Really? I thought jewellery was at resources 4 and 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T23:07:39-07:00","id":1337027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1337026#post1337026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Really? I thought jewellery was at resources 4 and 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the sort of regalia reserved for the Scarlet Empress would be worth Resources 5, but Creation is littered with princes and would-be princes who command Resources 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.th