edby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1337353#post1337353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think I should make a charm that should let them inflict mutations on animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly, no.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T14:18:16-07:00","id":1337370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1337361#post1337361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Mad scientists&amp;quot; are stock characters intended to showcase the perils of hubris and exploring forbidden knowledge. In the modern day, sure, that's a scientist, but the ancient pulp fantasy world depicted by Creation, that's absolutely a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Not particularly, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.... But how about a charm for exalted modern? We already have CRISPR and transgenic animals.<br /> <br /> Modern mad scientists is a valid character space, especially for a twilight. Maybe an animal escapes and starts to reproduce in the wild...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T14:23:16-07:00","id":1337371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1337370#post1337370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.... But how about a charm for exalted modern?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted Modern is not <i>our</i> world - it's a Creation that <i>looks like</i> our world, but still largely runs off many of the genre conventions that pervade Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1337370#post1337370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have CRISPR and transgenic animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in the world of Exalted Modern, there's probably some sorcery bound up in the origins of both of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-22-2019, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T14:49:48-07:00","id":1337379,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I disagree. Its not 'exalted modern' as shown in shards. Its 'modern earth, then exaltation starts popping up'. CRISPR and transgenic animals came from the same place as before, I.e. DNA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T15:07:08-07:00","id":1337383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1337379#post1337379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not 'exalted modern' as shown in shards. Its 'modern earth, then exaltation starts popping up'.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to make up random rules, it helps to lay them out at the start, rather than ask people what they think about your homebrew that hinges on said rules and <i>then</i> explain them when readers fail to divine your process.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, you probably shouldn't give your homebrew setting the same name as an official one, because it leads to precisely these kinds of misunderstandings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T15:29:42-07:00","id":1337385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1337383#post1337383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to make up random rules, it helps to lay them out at the start, rather than ask people what they think about your homebrew that hinges on said rules and <i>then</i> explain them when readers fail to divine your process.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, you probably shouldn't give your homebrew setting the same name as an official one, because it leads to precisely these kinds of misunderstandings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, fine. I'll start up another thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T15:45:23-07:00","id":1337390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1337385#post1337385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll start up another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not remotely what I asked for. Just next time, please, explain more about how you got to an idea before asking us what we think about the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T19:31:50-07:00","id":1337755,"title":"","content":"Brilliant Pilot Prana<br /> Cost: 2m<br /> Prereq: Excellency<br /> <br /> Mins: <br /> Drive/ Travel/ Sail/ Ride/ Fly: 3, Essence 2<br /> Duration: 1 hour<br /> Keyword: Obvious<br /> <br /> The solar's skill and ability in control of his vehicle shines through, regardless of circumstance. Whether it is riding a wounded horse, guiding a ship with a broken hull through a storm, or flying a plane whose engines have caught fire, the solar maneuvers unimpeded. This charm enables the solar to spend 1 mote to subtract one internal penalty, whether from a horse that is getting tired, damage, or running out of fuel. Glowing symbols proclaiming his excellence appear on the vehicle, while torn sails and destroyed engines reknit themselves or are replaced wholesale by glowing simulacrums. By the end of the duration, the solar either spends 2 motes again, or the constructs fall apart and the vehicle stalls. <br /> <br /> A/N: I based this kinda on 'There is no wind'. First of all, did I set the prerequisites too high? This is a dice adder trick, and it seems like bog-standard solar 'I am good no matter what' charms should be something that is easy to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:26:46-07:00","id":1339651,"title":"","content":"<b>Deficiency-mitigating prana of (Ability)</b><br /> Mins: Essence 2, 2 dots in the appopriate skill<br /> Cost:1m per device<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted surpass all boundaries and are excellent in all circumstances. This applies to their tools and equipment as well. This charm enables a solar to use a equipment as per normal, despite circumstances saying this should be impossible.<br /> <br /> For example, a solar can grab a rusted-out hulk of a car that has long since run out of fuel, and use it as if it was brand new. They can take a torchlight whose battery has run flat, and shine it into the darkness. A solar who is a craftsman, can use power tools, 3D printing machines, and electronic lathes, despite the power to the building being out. This applies to things like minor damage. Electricity runs through broken cables who have long since lost their insulation. Coolant and plasma run through cracked containment cells. Failing electronics are reinforced and do not fail.<br /> <br /> This costs 1 mote of essence to be commited per device, which extends to things like boats and cars. A repurchase at Essence 3 enables you to enhance 5 devices per mote committed, and another at essence 4 enables you to commit 10 motes for one building, whether it is an abandoned factory or a defunct hospital. <br /> <br /> The ability this charm is purchased for must apply. Craftsmen can boot up old CNC machiens and power saws. Linguists can activate old computers and let brush pens fill themselves with ink. Old sailors and drives can activate long defunct motorboats or cars. But a crafter will not be able to start up an engine, nor will a sniper be able to activate an MRI machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 10-08-2019, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T12:36:51-07:00","id":1339671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1339651#post1339651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Deficiency-mitigating prana</b><br /> Mins: Essence 1, any dot<br /> Cost:1m per device<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted surpass all boundaries ad are excellent in all circumstances. This applies to their tools and equipment as well. This charm enables a solar to use a equipment as per normal, despite circumstances saying this should be impossible. For example, a solar can grab a rusted-out hulk of a car that has long since run out of fuel, and use it as if it was brand new. They can take a torchlight whose battery has run flat, and shine it into the darkness. A solar who is a craftsman, can use power tools, 3D printing machines, and electronic lathes, despite the power to the building being out. This applies to things like minor damage. Electricity runs through broken cables who have long since lost their insulation. Coolant and plasma run through cracked containment cells. Failing electronics are reinforced and do not fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a craft charm building off of Durability-enhancing Technique. Or Crack-Mending Technique? Maybe both...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T13:03:27-07:00","id":1339683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1339671#post1339671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like a craft charm building off of Durability-enhancing Technique. Or Crack-Mending Technique? Maybe both...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Crack-mending technique is permanent and durability enhancing technique enhances hardness and soak. This is derived form god-mind algorithms, which enables any computer you touch to have a perfect battery and connection to the internet. This lets you use any form of advanced equipment which requires extensive infrastructure (e.g. electrical power) or extensive repairs, and lets you use it at least temporarily without problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T18:20:47-07:00","id":1339734,"title":"","content":"Then why not have it require God-Mind Algorithms as a prereq? As it is, you seem to have it be available to any Solar with a single dot in <i>any</i> skill. As it is, it kinda makes the Charm you're basing it off of pretty superfluous.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T01:03:30-07:00","id":1340174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1339734#post1339734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why not have it require God-Mind Algorithms as a prereq? As it is, you seem to have it be available to any Solar with a single dot in <i>any</i> skill. As it is, it kinda makes the Charm you're basing it off of pretty superfluous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... sorry then. I think I didn't quite do it very well. I think maybe it serve as an analogue to 'god mind algorithm' for any kind of skill, as long as it applies to what the solar is trying to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T09:16:28-07:00","id":1342720,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy charms for 2nd edition<br /> <br /> NATIVE SOLAR TALENT<br /> Occult 1, Essence 2<br /> The magics of the solar are mighty... But sometimes, they may take the time to learn the petty magics of thaumaturgy. This automatically drops the difficulty of any roll involving thaumaturgy by the solar's essence.<br /> <br /> RITUAL ENHANCING ARETE<br /> Occult 3, Essence 2<br /> The solar rolls what he would normally roll for a thaumaturical ritual, counting essence for auto successes. The successes can be used to enhance his occult result. Wards deal additional damage. Eagle eye potion grants more than 1 dice. Heavenly transmutation works faster and with more result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 10-21-2019, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T10:06:38-07:00","id":1342739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1342720#post1342720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NATIVE SOLAR TALENT<br /> Occult 1, Essence 2<br /> The magics of the solar are mighty... But sometimes, they may take the time to learn the petty magics of thaumaturgy. This automatically drops the difficulty of any roll involving thaumaturgy by the solar's essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many forms of thaumaturgy don't involve rolls at all, such as Unquenchable Flame, Speak With Ozashun, or Second Bread. And of the ones that do, dropping the Difficulty so sharply would make it pretty much effortless. Reading the future in someone's tea leaves, for instance, is only Difficulty 2, so this Charm would make it Difficulty 0 by default. Likewise Exorcism becomes drastically easier; no exaggeration here, an Essence 3 Solar with this Charm and the Excellency <i>and no other Charms</i> has a reasonable chance of forcing Octavian into a tree for a month and a day - at Essence 5 he's got a shot at forcing one of the Deathlords to retreat into the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-21-2019, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T10:17:43-07:00","id":1342742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1342739#post1342739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many forms of thaumaturgy don't involve rolls at all, such as Unquenchable Flame, Speak With Ozashun, or Second Bread. And of the ones that do, dropping the Difficulty so sharply would make it pretty much effortless. Reading the future in someone's tea leaves, for instance, is only Difficulty 2, so this Charm would make it Difficulty 0 by default. Likewise Exorcism becomes drastically easier; no exaggeration here, an Essence 3 Solar with this Charm and the Excellency <i>and no other Charms</i> has a reasonable chance of forcing Octavian into a tree for a month and a day - at Essence 5 he's got a shot at forcing one of the Deathlords to retreat into the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Made some edits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T15:56:17-08:00","id":1346306,"title":"","content":"There was a time in sufficient velocity where craftsman needs no tools made the game a bit too boring. As in, solars were human heroes. They were tool users. They shouldn't bypass tools entirely, but start with enhancing what they already had.<br /> <br /> So... <br /> <br /> GADGET ENHANCING PRANA<br /> Mins: Essence 1, 1 dot in the relative ability<br /> Cost: 2m<br /> Duration: scene long<br /> The solar's excellence flows around her, entering the tools by which she enacts her will. This enhances her tools and whatever she is using. No matter the type, as long as it is usable, the tool will increase in ability and usefulness, in the form of a 3 dice bonus in the abilty roll, whether it is a sewing machine, sword, or car. The solar can enhance (Willpower x 2) tools this way. <br /> <br /> MECHANISM AMPLIFYING ARETE<br /> Mins: Essence 2, 3 dots in relevant ability<br /> Duration: 1 day<br /> Cost: 5m<br /> Prereq: gadget enhancing prana<br /> <br /> This upgrades its prerequisite, making it last for a day. This Charm transforms the 3 dice bonus coming from equipment to change into 3 successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T17:07:12-08:00","id":1346322,"title":"","content":"Giving yourself the equivalent of six dice to all relevant uses of a dice pool for a day for seven committed motes is, ah, one of those things that could throw game balance out of whack again. Like, there's no easy access to an effect like 2e's Infinite (Ability) Mastery in Ex3 for a reason.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T17:08:36-08:00","id":1346323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1346322#post1346322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving yourself the equivalent of six dice to all relevant uses of a dice pool for a day for seven committed motes is, ah, one of those things that could throw game balance out of whack again. Like, there's no easy access to an effect like 2e's Infinite (Ability) Mastery in Ex3 for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, then.... <br /> <br /> Maybe an addendum that says 'alter the charm dice however you want. The concept stays the same'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T19:25:33-08:00","id":1346332,"title":"","content":"Why not offer tools double 9's or some such instead of more dice? It gives you access to more successes without just inflating a dice pool. Or reroll 1's, or another dice trick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T19:54:59-08:00","id":1346336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1346332#post1346332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not offer tools double 9's or some such instead of more dice? It gives you access to more successes without just inflating a dice pool. Or reroll 1's, or another dice trick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well..... here's a thing. <br /> <br /> I got no fucking idea how those dice tricks work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T21:54:16-08:00","id":1346364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1346336#post1346336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well..... here's a thing. <br /> <br /> I got no fucking idea how those dice tricks work.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to be hostile.<br /> <br /> The basic dice roll assumes that a 7, 8, or 9 counts as a success, while 10 counts as two successes. Other results are not successes, and a 1 means that if there are no successes, the roll is a botch.<br /> <br /> Dice tricks mess with that. <br /> <br /> So \u201cDouble 9s\u201d means that nines also count as two successes. \u201cDouble 8s\u201d means that eights <i>and</i> nines also count as two successes. \u201cDouble 7s\u201d means that sevens, eights, and nines all count as two successes.<br /> <br /> \u201cReroll 1s\u201d would mean that you reroll the ones. \u201cReroll 1s until they cease to appear\u201d would mean that you reroll the ones and, if any of <i>those</i> turn up ones, reroll them, and keep at it until you don\u2019t have any ones left.<br /> <br /> Some dice tricks care about the result of the opponent\u2019s roll - for instance, you might add an extra die to your roll for every 1 that comes up in their roll.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s actually pretty intuitive, and it\u2019s a lot better for the game than just pumping dice pools to insane levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T22:09:53-08:00","id":1346368,"title":"","content":"Apologies. No hostility was meant. <br /> <br /> Ok, let me get this straight...<br /> <br /> 'reroll 1s' mean that you can't botch this roll. <br /> <br /> 'double 7/8/9' means that the number of successes you obtain are larger. The smaller the number you double, the better off you are. <br /> <br /> This probably doesn't get through my head because I usually just halve the number of dice and count them as successes in my head. <br /> <br /> Fine, then. I'll alter the thing a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T22:25:31-08:00","id":1346372,"title":"","content":"It matters much more when you are actually rolling dice, if you are doing math as dice, then nothing beats a bigger pool but also the biggest pool always wins. If I were you I'd use a random number generator to make rolls to add back in random elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T22:40:58-08:00","id":1346376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1346372#post1346372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It matters much more when you are actually rolling dice, if you are doing math as dice, then nothing beats a bigger pool but also the biggest pool always wins. If I were you I'd use a random number generator to make rolls to add back in random elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I should start using one. I am writing a story. <br /> <br /> Got recommendations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T23:43:26-08:00","id":1346386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://qrng.anu.edu.au/Lucky.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://qrng.anu.edu.au/Lucky.php</a> This is done with quantum physics. It is as random as you can create with a computer. Or just ask google, it will roll dice for you, or buy real dice. I think the Onyx path app supports exalted but I just roll real dice normally. I have a big bag of d10 mostly for Exalted. It is crazy when your players roll 30+ dice at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T00:45:10-08:00","id":1347632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1346386#post1346386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://qrng.anu.edu.au/Lucky.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://qrng.anu.edu.au/Lucky.php</a> This is done with quantum physics. It is as random as you can create with a computer. Or just ask google, it will roll dice for you, or buy real dice. I think the Onyx path app supports exalted but I just roll real dice normally. I have a big bag of d10 mostly for Exalted. It is crazy when your players roll 30+ dice at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I just tried it out.<br /> <br /> The buttons appear to be unresponsive.<br /> <br /> edit: Apologies, that was wrong. A list of numbers came out. <br /> <br /> Set 1: 1<br /> Set 2: 1<br /> Set 3: 2<br /> Set 4: 2<br /> Set 5: 0<br /> Set 6: 1<br /> Set 7: 0<br /> Set 8: 7<br /> Set 9: 4<br /> Set 10: 8<br /> <br /> Which ever exalt rolled this is in for a bad day....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T01:42:57-08:00","id":1347637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1347632#post1347632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">edit: Apologies, that was wrong. A list of numbers came out.<br /> <br /> Set 1: 1<br /> Set 2: 1<br /> Set 3: 2<br /> Set 4: 2<br /> Set 5: <b>0</b><br /> Set 6: 1<br /> Set 7: <b>0</b><br /> Set 8: <b>7</b><br /> Set 9: 4<br /> Set 10: <b>8</b><br /> <br /> Which ever exalt rolled this is in for a bad day....</div> </div> </div> </div>You call six successes on ten dice &quot;a bad day?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T01:58:32-08:00","id":1347641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1347637#post1347637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You call six successes on ten dice &amp;quot;a bad day?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I miscalculated. Saw a number below 7, so ignored it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T02:08:38-08:00","id":1347643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1347641#post1347641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saw a number below 7, so ignored it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but the dice have ten sides. Try setting the minimum to 1 instead of 0, and the maximum to 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-11-2019, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T02:04:16-08:00","id":1348814,"title":"","content":"Thanks man.<br /> <br /> OK it's a transgression that solars can't do a flash impression. At least for 2e.<br /> <br /> Lets make some stuff<br /> <br /> FLASHING MOVEMENT PRANA<br /> Mins: athletics 2, essence 2<br /> Duration: indefinite<br /> Prereqs: lightning speed<br /> Keyword: combo ok<br /> <br /> The solars move like the sun itself. Swift and unstopping. Like the rays of light, moving across the sky at impossible speed. The dash and movement ratings of the solar are permanently altered, and are now doubled. <br /> <br /> UNSTOPPABLE FLASHING MOVEMENT<br /> Mins: athletics 3, essence 3<br /> Duration: a scene<br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Prereq: flashing movement prana<br /> Keyword: combo ok<br /> <br /> The solars move like lightning, each footstep the thunderous crash of the world's mightiest warriors charging against the armies of the pirmordials. The solars movement rate is now multiplied by 5 times over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T02:34:01-08:00","id":1348817,"title":"","content":"So long as you realize this is horribly broken. Like massively, horribly broken beyond any hope of saving (unless the speed doesn't stack with other sources and turns off in combat, maybe -- even then).<br /> <br /> Cannoicly, an Eclipse-oid (I did it with an Essence 10 Fiend) can reach a max speed of 1920 Yards Per Tick on a Reflexive Flying Dash (that's 3927MPH and a little over Mach 5, or 26 yards/tick walking which shenningans into 106 miles per hour indefinite marching speed, or 548mph indefinite running). So (Post Crisis Wally) Flash speed is possible 2E RAW... but it's <i>hard</i>. <br /> <br /> And it's hard to stop backpeddling archers. Increasing speed like this breaks the game. (And god help you if an Eclipse-oid gets their hands on this -- double speed plus five-times speed on Mach 5.16.... *drool*.)<br /> <br /> Likewise it's possible to hit Strength+Athletics of 93 for Feats of Strength (which conservatively is at least lift 21 tons without a roll). But it's hard because that's not what Exalted is about. It's magically enhanced skill, not static superpowers.<br /> <br /> (You can also reach unbound speeds in a race or when facing a deadline but I don't count those. The Prince of Iron and Fire also had Telescopic, Microscopic, Mass Pentrating (i.e. xray) vision by the end of that campaign. Man that was fun. He also shot lazer beams from his eyes and wore a cape, but that's totally not what Exalted (even 2E) is supposed to be about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-16-2019, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T03:26:35-08:00","id":1348824,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I know this is pretty much bullshit. I just think that solars should be able to go really fucking fast.<br /> <br /> A question. What if you take the eclipse out of the equation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T06:09:32-08:00","id":1348842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1348824#post1348824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know this is pretty much bullshit. I just think that solars should be able to go really fucking fast.<br /> <br /> A question. What if you take the eclipse out of the equation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you faster than your enemies, and do you have ranged attacks?<br /> <br /> If so, still broken.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> In play, it's fixable. Force fights close quarters and blocked lines of sight (like in dungeons). Give the PCs reasons to stay put. But it's powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-16-2019, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T06:12:13-08:00","id":1348845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1348842#post1348842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you faster than your enemies, and do you have ranged attacks?<br /> <br /> If so, still broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt that pretty much the case for, well, everything? I mean, I can say the same thing for the game being broken if someone who invested in melee beats someone who invested in medicine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T06:16:43-08:00","id":1348846,"title":"","content":"Right. But that doesn't mean a Melee Charm that gives you a Permenant Perfect Defence isn't broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T06:17:26-08:00","id":1348847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1348845#post1348845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isnt that pretty much the case for, well, everything?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. <span style=\"color:White\">/10char</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T06:29:57-08:00","id":1348850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1348846#post1348846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. But that doesn't mean a Melee Charm that gives you a Permenant Perfect Defence isn't broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can beat this defense. Get a charm that counterattack ranged attacks with an infinite range counterattack. Move faster. Surprise the archery solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T06:32:50-08:00","id":1348851,"title":"","content":"And Heavenly Guardian Defence needs a weapon and has a Flaw of Invulnerablity -- it's beatable too but still broken as a free permenant Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T00:13:45-08:00","id":1349012,"title":"","content":"Fine, then. I don't get it. but I respect your opinion anyway. <br /> <br /> Does a stunt to make your anima light up so you can read at night count as a charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T00:50:07-08:00","id":1349017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1349012#post1349012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fine, then. I don't get it. but I respect your opinion anyway. <br /> <br /> Does a stunt to make your anima light up so you can read at night count as a charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E and 2E it's a basic anima power. Spend 1m to light up. Not a Charm.<br /> <br /> In 3E you can only make your Castemark appear for 1m. I guess lighting up could be a Charm. Or you could just burn 5m to get to Glowing. Until you made this post I didn't even realise you couldn't light up as a basic anima power anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T05:00:19-08:00","id":1350793,"title":"","content":"SWIFT LANGUAGE ACQUISITION ACTION<br /> Linguistics 2, Essence 2<br /> Cost: 5m <br /> Minimums: Linguistics excellency<br /> Duration: 1 month<br /> <br /> The Solar's reach far and wide, and the their domains encompass vast countries. It is, of course, imperative that she learns their language, better for them to share in her glory and wisdom. This encompasses a dramatic action where the solar reads a book, travels alongside those who know the language, or simply meditates on the people who he wishes to communicate with. At the end, he learns the language, speaking in whatever native accent that is local. After one month, the memory of the langauge fades, and he can no longer speak it.*<br /> <br /> *I don't care if it is better than the canon charm. No way is a solar going to be worse than a dragonblooded at rapidly acquiring new langauges. <br /> <br /> Conveying the Ideal word. <br /> Linguistics 4, Essence 3<br /> Cost: Permanent<br /> Prereqs: Poetic expression style<br /> <br /> All langauges have a root. All languages have a similarity. All langugages, from West to South to East to North, each have a similarity due to them all deviating from the root language. The platonic form of all languages, the ideal word. The solar knows this word, and uses it to convey information he needs. Anything he writes or speaks, is instantly understood by anyone who can perceive it, as if it was in their own native language. This ideal word can be copied by scribes and replayed by audio recorders, but in itself it cannot be used by mortals, the intricacies and subtleties of the language too vast for their minds to comprehend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T06:13:09-08:00","id":1350803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350793#post1350793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No way is a solar going to be worse than a dragonblooded at rapidly acquiring new langauges.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not, though. Consider how the Dragon-Blooded who wants to learn languages spends at least one day (but possibly as many as five) learning the language, and then spends five motes, at which point he can understand its spoken and written forms. He still can't speak it unless he has Linguistics 4+, Essence 2+, and takes off <b>three successes</b> from all social influence rolls to use it. And his knowledge of the language lasts for <b>one scene</b>.<br /> <br /> What makes you think Excellent Emissary's Tongue is deficient by comparison?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350793#post1350793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conveying the Ideal word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise, what's wrong with Single Voice Kata?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-25-2019, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T06:52:13-08:00","id":1350813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350803#post1350803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not, though. Consider how the Dragon-Blooded who wants to learn languages spends at least one day (but possibly as many as five) learning the language, and then spends five motes, at which point he can understand its spoken and written forms. He still can't speak it unless he has Linguistics 4+, Essence 2+, and takes off <b>three successes</b> from all social influence rolls to use it. And his knowledge of the language lasts for <b>one scene</b>.<br /> <br /> What makes you think Excellent Emissary's Tongue is deficient by comparison?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably not so much that the Solar Charm is weaker but rather that the Solar must be Essence 3 to use it whereas a DB can start learning new languages as soon as E1.<br /> <br /> You might argue that a Solar doesn't <b>need</b> to learn the languages before E3 because they can universally understand spoken word and universally communicate with word or body language. But the Solar still can't understand written word before E3, the DB can actually learn the language while the Solar is &quot;stuck&quot; relying on their omnitongue until then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350803#post1350803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, what's wrong with Single Voice Kata?</div> </div> </div> </div>His version can be written down and recorded and it doesn't offend spirits and fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T07:03:44-08:00","id":1350815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350813#post1350813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably not so much that the Solar Charm is weaker but rather that the Solar must be Essence 3 to use it whereas a DB can start learning new languages as soon as E1.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar also has the option to do so at Essence 1 if he takes Linguistics Supernal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350813#post1350813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Solar still can't understand written word before E3, the DB can actually learn the language...</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it count as &quot;learning&quot; the language if you only understand it for the scene you use the Charm, and can't speak it?<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, the Dragon-Blooded can take the time outside the Charm being active to improve his understanding of a tongue until he's internalized it well enough to no longer need to crystallize it with Essence in his mind... but so can the Solar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350813#post1350813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His version can be written down and recorded and it doesn't offend spirits and fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but those seemed like pretty reasonable limitations in the original. Is there a reason for removing them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T07:24:29-08:00","id":1350816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350815#post1350815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar also has the option to do so at Essence 1 if he takes Linguistics Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty steep requirement which a DB doesn't have. If we start balancing non-Solar splats by comparing with a Solar supernal for every ability, then all the splats are gonna get a power boost something fierce.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350815#post1350815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it count as &quot;learning&quot; the language if you only understand it for the scene you use the Charm, and can't speak it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it does. That E1 DB will be able to decypher a first age tablet of lost knowledge that an E1 Solar won't be able to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T07:27:35-08:00","id":1350817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350815#post1350815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar also has the option to do so at Essence 1 if he takes Linguistics Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop.<br /> <br /> This is stupid. A supernal is something that is vital to the character. It is a literal core to what they are. <br /> <br /> You do not take a supernal for the sake of 'I can learn languages fast when I travel abroad'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T07:29:01-08:00","id":1350818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350815#post1350815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but those seemed like pretty reasonable limitations in the original. Is there a reason for removing them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a better idea. Why not create a language bypass charm that doesn't piss off elementals and gods, whom you might need to speak with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T07:43:32-08:00","id":1350821,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> can you dial back the confrontational tone please?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350818#post1350818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's a better idea. Why not create a language bypass charm that doesn't piss off elementals and gods, whom you might need to speak with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the reason for the limitation is to preserve the niche of Ancient Tongue Understanding, which is the actual &quot;speak with any spirit&quot; Charm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T08:38:23-08:00","id":1350829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350816#post1350816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes it does. That E1 DB will be able to decypher a first age tablet of lost knowledge that an E1 Solar won't be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>But he won't be able to order drinks, ask where the bathroom is, or talk his way out of a magistrate's fines, all of which an E1 Solar who doesn't even bother taking Linguistics as his Supernal <i>can</i> do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350817#post1350817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stop.<br /> <br /> This is stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself in agreement with Epitome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350817#post1350817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A supernal is something that is vital to the character. It is a literal core to what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350817#post1350817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not take a supernal for the sake of 'I can learn languages fast when I travel abroad'</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that what a character takes as his Supernal can vary pretty drastically based on the goals of the player and the table around him. In a game that's going to be focused around travel and bringing people together, that might be <i>exactly</i> why a player takes Linguistics Supernal.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Incidentally, one of the other players in my group also took Linguistics as her Supernal, but that was because being an awesome novelist is the core of her concept. Why is &quot;author&quot; valid but &quot;linguist&quot; not?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-25-2019, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T08:41:08-08:00","id":1358201,"title":"","content":"Apologies if I get this wrong.<br /> <br /> Absurd Iron Body Prana<br /> Essence: 2<br /> Resistance: 3<br /> <br /> It is not enough that those who attack the lawgivers fail in their affront. They must also be disciplined. After all, those who come too close to the sun burn up. This supplements a resistance roll. When the character is struck by a melee attack and successfully blocks all damage, he may use this charm reflexively to destroy the weapon of the attacker, rolling resistance against the targets essence, with (essence) autosuccesses. The weapon is rendered into useless slag, or if it was a natural weapon, burned into uselessness as a temporary crippling effect. <br /> <br /> At essence 3, a repurchase allows him detonate the weapon with a deadly conflagration, molten shards leaping for the vital organs in a manner not unlike a grenade. At essence 4, this applies to ranged weapons as well.<br /> <br /> Artifact weapons are immune to this effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T11:00:20-08:00","id":1358224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1350816#post1350816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it does. That E1 DB will be able to decypher a first age tablet of lost knowledge that an E1 Solar won't be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>And an Essence 1 Lunar can fly whilst the Solar can't.<br /> <br /> Solars don't have to be better than every splat in every area at every Essence/XP commitment level.<br /> <br /> It's ok that other splats access powers earlier or easier than Solars. Deebs were made to be lieutenants and major domos. They exist now at the head of a massive Empire. Rough and ready translation doesn't seem out of theme to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T16:18:41-08:00","id":1358294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1358224#post1358224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And an Essence 1 Lunar can fly whilst the Solar can't.<br /> <br /> Solars don't have to be better than every splat in every area at every Essence/XP commitment level.<br /> <br /> It's ok that other splats access powers earlier or easier than Solars. Deebs were made to be lieutenants and major domos. They exist now at the head of a massive Empire. Rough and ready translation doesn't seem out of theme to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with it myself. To make my position clearer, I was defending the point that DBs can be better than Solars at acquiring new languages at early Essence, not the opinion that this is a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:00:08-08:00","id":1358313,"title":"","content":"BE THE CHANGE YOU WANT TO SEE IN THE WORLD PRANA<br /> Essence: 3<br /> Performance 4<br /> Keywords: Permanent<br /> <br /> The solar's very presence exemplifies the very ideals he loves so much. Upon the taking of this charm, the solar chooses one ideal, which he then follows. From then on, a scene where he acts in a manner fitting the ideal, counts as a scene spent building up a major intimacy to that ideal. For example, if a solar was to chose the ideal of sharing and helping the poor, whether in the slums or at a gala, his attempts to raise funds or distribute food would lead to anyone coming into contact with him to be affected by this charm. A solar who chose 'equality' as his ideal, and treated both Brahmins and Undesirables with the same respect and care, would instill a desire to treat everyone equally in any who see this occuring. <br /> <br /> At essence 4, a repurchase allows this to occur anyone receiving news of the solar. Whether from television, documents and reporters praising him, or via stories of his legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:16:38-08:00","id":1358318,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s already something like that in Sun King Radiance, except the recipient may <i>voluntarily</i> accept the Intimacy. I feel like getting to automatically force Major charitable Principles on people just by tipping one\u2019s waitress seems a bit much even for an Essence 3 Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:19:57-08:00","id":1358319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1358318#post1358318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s already something like that in Sun King Radiance, except the recipient may <i>voluntarily</i> accept the Intimacy. I feel like getting to automatically force Major charitable Principles on people just by tipping one\u2019s waitress seems a bit much even for an Essence 3 Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Automatically force? But.... it basically means like talking. Instead of making a speech on charitableness, you just act as you are, and people are inspired by uou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:39:02-08:00","id":1358322,"title":"","content":"People don\u2019t get Major Principles just from you talking to them, either, though - to Instill someone with a Major Intimacy, first you have to Instill them with a Minor, <i>then</i> Instill them again, using another Intimacy they already possess to reinforce the one you\u2019re trying to upgrade to Major. And both times, you have to overcome their Resolve, and they can spend Willpower to overcome it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T19:13:13-08:00","id":1358327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335043-a-fistful-of-charms?p=1358322#post1358322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People don\u2019t get Major Principles just from you talking to them, either, though - to Instill someone with a Major Intimacy, first you have to Instill them with a Minor, <i>then</i> Instill them again, using another Intimacy they already possess to reinforce the one you\u2019re trying to upgrade to Major. And both times, you have to overcome their Resolve, and they can spend Willpower to overcome it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this? Your very presence works out the same. But Essence 3, gives you minor. Essence 4, gives you major. And essence 5, gives you defining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T19:46:25-08:00","id":1358333,"title":"","content":"I still don\u2019t care for the Essence 